vyatta-kdump (0.3danos5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Test-only change; no change to the shipped binaries or config.
  * The revert test fixtures now use the test process's own euid/egid as
    the snapshot's env file owner instead of a hard-coded 0:0, so the
    revert tests also pass when built as a non-root user (as on OBS).
    Restoring the saved owner still calls chown unchanged; that path stays
    covered by the two root-only cases TestRevertRestoresOwner and
    TestRevertReplayRestoresOwnerModeBytesTwice.

 -- i-danos dev <dev@i-danos.dev>  Sun, 25 Oct 2026 21:12:23 -0700

vyatta-kdump (0.3danos4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Apply is observable and self-reverting (A02 phase 3): applyConfig takes
    a snapshot of grubenv crashkernel memory, the kdump service state, the
    kexec crash-kernel flag and /etc/default/kdump-tools, and on any error
    reverts in reverse order, reporting every step. A snapshot failure
    aborts before anything is changed and a revert never deletes an env file
    that merely could not be read.
  * Disable no longer swallows the service-stop error, GrubReservedMem
    distinguishes "unset" from "command failed", and a nil configuration is
    treated as disabled with cleanup instead of dereferencing nil.
  * Config and cache do not advance after a failed or reverted apply.
  * Not restored (by design): xattrs/ACLs/labels and timestamps of the env
    file, the crash kernel already loaded, and the running crashkernel=
    command line (reboot-only).
  * Unit tests for each snapshot input, revert path and the marshal format.
  * Version note: danos2 and danos3 were intermediate local builds and were
    never published.

 -- i-danos dev <dev@i-danos.dev>  Fri, 23 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0700

